@title After-Hours Care Options
@subtitle Decision page for the partners, 2026-11-04
@author Odette Rousseau, Practice Manager

Larch Valley Medical Group has 38,000 patients. We want to add after-hours care.

## Options
cards
### Extended clinic hours until 21:00
- Annual cost: $410,000
- About 900 visits a month
- Average wait: 25 minutes
- Can handle any visit that needs an exam

### Telehealth urgent care
- Annual cost: $260,000
- About 1500 visits a month
- Average wait: 12 minutes
- Cannot handle visits that need a physical exam

### Nurse triage phone line, 17:00 to 23:00
- Annual cost: $185,000
- About 2200 calls a month
- Calls answered within 3 minutes
- The vendor estimates it avoids 18% of emergency room referrals

## Cost per contact
data cost = option,usd; Extended hours,38; Telehealth,14; Nurse triage,7
chart hbar cost unit=$ title="Cost per contact"

Extended hours is the most expensive per contact, but it is the only option that treats patients who need an exam.

## What each can and cannot do
- Extended hours: any visit, including those that need an exam.
- Telehealth urgent care: visits that do not need a physical exam. It cannot handle visits that need one.
- Nurse triage line: calls answered within 3 minutes, with an estimated 18% of emergency room referrals avoided.

## Recommendation
Start with the telehealth urgent care service now. Add the nurse triage line in the second half of 2027. Keep extended hours under consideration if telehealth use is low.

!! The partners need to approve the $260,000 telehealth budget on 2026-11-04.
